# lgdemo: Tea + Lipgloss integration demo under a real pty (M-FOUNDATION S7).
#
# Frame layout at cols=80 (then cols=40), 6 rows per frame — a Lipgloss
# rounded-border box (cyan edges) with padding 1 and width = cols, around a
# bold-cyan "lgdemo" title rendered NESTED in the content (the box's align
# math skips its ANSI) plus the live model line:
#   \e[?25l  (first paint only)
#   \e[2K\e[36m╭─…╮\e[0m\r\n
#   \e[2K\e[36m│\e[0m<cols spaces>\e[36m│\e[0m\r\n            (pad row, x2)
#   \e[2K\e[36m│\e[0m \e[1;36mlgdemo\e[0m<pad>\e[36m│\e[0m\r\n
#   \e[2K\e[36m│\e[0m n=<k> last=<key> size=<c>x<r> <pad>\e[36m│\e[0m\r\n
#   \e[2K\e[36m╰─…╯\e[0m\r\n
# repaints are prefixed \e[6A (move up 6).
#
# Every directive is settled by an expect BEFORE the next fires — no two
# events are ever pending at once (the host drains a pending SIGWINCH before
# pending keys, so back-to-back directives would make frame order racy).
# Needles name bytes that exist only in the frame they await: the first
# paint's head, a changed n=/last= field, the 40-wide top edge (the 80-wide
# edge cannot contain it: after 40 dashes comes dash 41, never ╮), and the
# exit path's showCursor.
expect \e[?25l\e[2K\e[36m╭
send x
expect n=1 last=x size=80x24
resize 40 12
expect \e[36m╭────────────────────────────────────────╮\e[0m
expect n=1 last=x size=40x12
send y
expect n=2 last=y size=40x12
send \r
expect \e[?25h
expect_exit 0
